## 3. Exact bounded operation contract

### 3.1 Process envelope and preconditions

The approved run must begin in the literal execution working directory from
Section 2 and may not change directory. It must use a non-interactive shell
with an empty inherited environment except for the following literal variables.
It must use GIT_DIR=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git,
GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects,
GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES empty, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1,
GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, HOME=/nonexistent, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0,
GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, GIT_PAGER=cat, LC_ALL=C, and PATH=/usr/bin:/bin.
The harness does not invoke git config or parse a configuration value as data;
Git's own internal repository metadata parsing for object lookup is constrained
to this literal Git directory, emits no value, and is not a permitted output
source. It may not invoke git config, git status, git worktree, git checkout,
git sparse-checkout, git archive, git show, git log, git grep, git fsck, git
fetch, git pull, git push, or any network command.

Before the first Git command, all of these conditions are required:

    test "$(pwd -P)" = /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace
    test -d /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox
    test -d /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git
    test ! -L /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git
    test -d /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects
    test ! -L /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects
    test ! -L /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects/info
    test ! -e /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects/info/alternates
    test ! -L /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects/info/alternates
    test ! -e /tmp/agents-os-phase5d-m0d-object-only-source-run-555b3b538f6e
    test ! -L /tmp/agents-os-phase5d-m0d-object-only-source-run-555b3b538f6e
    test ! -e /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/control-plane/registry/receipts/2026-07-25-yellow-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-v0.1.yaml
    test ! -L /home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/control-plane/registry/receipts/2026-07-25-yellow-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-v0.1.yaml

The runner must then create only the literal run root with mode 0700 and write
the ownership marker with exactly these two LF-terminated lines:

    run_id=PHASE5D_M0D_ACTUAL_OBJECT_ONLY_SOURCE_RUN_20260725_V0_1
    sealed_commit=555b3b538f6eb736e530c2912de678c5941f9985

No source bytes, tree output, Git stderr, environment values, configuration
contents, protected path names, or source-path list may be written below the run
root.

### 3.2 Protected-name-only scan

This scan is permitted because it consumes tree entry names only. It never asks
Git for a protected object ID, mode, blob type, or blob content. It must read
the complete name-only stream in memory, compare the protected-name subset to
the following exact ordered inventory, and emit no name:

    Plugin/CodeSearcher/config.env
    Plugin/DailyNote/config.env
    Plugin/FileOperator/config.env
    Plugin/LinuxShellExecutor/config.env
    Plugin/MagiAgent/config.env
    Plugin/NCBIDatasets/config.env
    Plugin/PowerShellExecutor/config.env

The scanner must treat a path as protected if its basename is .env, begins
.env., equals config.env, ends in .pem or .key, or any path component equals
credentials, tokens, cookies, secret, secrets, or state-private. The complete
protected subset must equal the seven rows above in that order. An absent,
renamed, extra, reordered, or duplicate protected name is a failure. The
scanner may return only a zero/nonzero exit status to its caller; it must not
print its input, an error message, or an inventory.

The one permitted Git producer for that scanner is exactly:

    git --git-dir=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git ls-tree -r --name-only -z 555b3b538f6eb736e530c2912de678c5941f9985 -- 2>/dev/null

Its stdout is connected only to the in-memory scanner stdin. Its stderr is
discarded. This is a whole-tree name-only scan, not generic tree/blob
enumeration: no object IDs or blob bytes are requested for any path in the
stream.

### 3.3 Exact Git command inventory

Every Git command below has stdout captured only into an internal scalar or
piped directly to a SHA-256 program. Every command has stderr redirected to
/dev/null. No captured scalar may be written to a terminal, log, temporary
file, or final receipt.

G01 proves only that the frozen commit object exists:

    git --git-dir=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git cat-file -e 555b3b538f6eb736e530c2912de678c5941f9985^{commit} >/dev/null 2>/dev/null

G02 obtains the frozen commit tree into an internal scalar, which must equal the
sealed tree literal:

    git --git-dir=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git rev-parse 555b3b538f6eb736e530c2912de678c5941f9985^{tree} 2>/dev/null

G03 is the exact name-only producer in Section 3.2.

Each tuple has exactly three calls: resolve its path against the sealed commit,
assert that the resulting object is a blob, and pipe only that already-matched
allowlisted blob to SHA-256. The resolve call must equal the row OID before its
type or byte-digest call is made.

