## 4. Sanitized output and owned cleanup finalizer

### 4.1 Output suppression

The only allowed persistent output is the exact final receipt target in Section
2. It is written only after the finalizer has run. It must use UTF-8, LF-only
line endings and contain only:

    schema_version
    run_id
    package_sha256
    sealed_commit
    sealed_tree
    tuple_set_preimage_sha256
    tuple_count
    protected_name_inventory_preimage_sha256
    protected_name_count
    protected_blob_content_reads
    allowlisted_blob_content_reads
    Git_command_count
    Host_operation_count
    worktree_created
    payload_files_created
    stdout_bytes_emitted
    stderr_bytes_emitted
    cleanup_status
    result
    failure_phase

The receipt may not contain source bytes, source excerpts, any individual path,
object ID, content digest, raw Git output, raw stderr, environment value,
repository configuration value, protected-path name, or stack trace. The caller
receives only the process exit code and the receipt path; normal stdout and
stderr remain empty.

Success requires these exact output assertions:

    tuple_count: 7
    protected_name_count: 7
    protected_blob_content_reads: 0
    allowlisted_blob_content_reads: 7
    Git_command_count: 24
    Host_operation_count: 0
    worktree_created: false
    payload_files_created: 0
    stdout_bytes_emitted: 0
    stderr_bytes_emitted: 0
    cleanup_status: CLEAN
    result: OBJECT_ONLY_SOURCE_RUN_EVIDENCE_CANDIDATE_ONLY
    failure_phase: null

### 4.2 Finalizer

The finalizer runs after both success and every failure that occurs after the
literal run root is created. It may touch only the literal run root and its two
known regular files: the ownership marker and temporary result. It must:

1. read the marker only to compare it byte-for-byte with the two literal lines
   in Section 3.1;
2. remove the marker and temporary result by their exact literal paths;
3. use rmdir on the literal run root; and
4. verify that the run root no longer exists and is not a symlink.

It must not use rm -rf, recursive deletion, globbing, parent traversal,
caller-supplied paths, a worktree cleanup command, or a Host cleanup method.

If the marker is missing or differs, a known temporary file is missing, rmdir
fails, or the run root still exists, the result is
BLOCKED_CLEANUP_OR_RESIDUE_UNVERIFIED. The runner must stop. It may write only
the sanitized failure receipt; it may not try a broader deletion.

## 5. Fail-closed results and review gate

| Condition | Required terminal result |
| --- | --- |
| Any required path exists, is a symlink, or cannot be owned exclusively | BLOCKED_PREEXISTING_OR_UNOWNED_PATH |
| Git executable or required local utility unavailable | BLOCKED_LOCAL_TOOLING_UNAVAILABLE |
| G01 fails, G02 tree differs, or a tuple does not resolve/type/digest exactly | BLOCKED_SEALED_SOURCE_OR_TUPLE_MISMATCH |
| Name-only scanner detects any protected inventory deviation | BLOCKED_PROTECTED_PATH_INVENTORY_MISMATCH |
| Any output leaves the allowed sink or a forbidden Git command is attempted | BLOCKED_UNAUTHORIZED_OR_NONHERMETIC_GIT_OPERATION |
| Any worktree, checkout, archive, sparse checkout, payload, plugin, Host, runtime, database, provider, auth, private Memory, sensing, recording, or effect attempt occurs | BLOCKED_OUT_OF_SCOPE_OPERATION |
| Finalizer cannot prove clean owned-root removal | BLOCKED_CLEANUP_OR_RESIDUE_UNVERIFIED |
| All preconditions and exact operations pass | OBJECT_ONLY_SOURCE_RUN_EVIDENCE_CANDIDATE_ONLY |

This package is not execution-ready merely because it exists. Before Section 6
can be consumed, a fresh independent review must verify:

1. all frozen input hashes in Section 2;
2. all seven tuple rows and both inventory fingerprints;
3. that the command inventory has no worktree, checkout, archive, sparse,
   protected-object, dynamic-path, output-leak, or Host operation;
4. that the name-only scanner cannot expose protected names or inspect protected
   object identifiers or contents;
5. that the finalizer cannot expand beyond the literal newly owned run root;
6. that a preexisting path, tuple substitution, protected-name substitution,
   extra Git call, output leak, and cleanup failure each fail closed; and
7. that no VCPToolBox command was executed while creating or reviewing this
   package.

Only PASS_NO_BLOCKER from that review can make this package eligible for a
current Jenn Section 6 A decision. It still cannot make a Host-smoke decision
eligible.

## 6. Jenn decision surface

### A. Authorize exactly one actual object-only source run

Exact decision text:

    我确认执行 AGENTS OS Phase 5D M0-D Actual Object-Only Source Run Decision
    Package v0.1 第 6 节 A 的完整 Exact decision text。

    我只授权一次、只使用本包第 2 节的 canonical VCPToolBox root、sealed commit、
    sealed tree、literal run root、receipt target 与完整 7 个 tuple，以及第 3 节 G01–G03
    和 T01–T07 的精确 Git command inventory。允许的 source bytes 仅可从七个已匹配 tuple
    经由 Git cat-file blob 流入 SHA-256；不得输出、保存或解释这些 bytes。保护路径只可进行
    name-only 内存比对，不得读取其 object ID、内容、哈希或配置语义。

    我确认本次不授权 git worktree、checkout、sparse checkout、archive、fetch、network、
    plugin、PluginManager、discovery、load、initialize、shutdown、processToolCall、native/N-API、
    runtime、database、provider、authentication、private Memory、state-private、sensing、recording
    或任何真实 effect。不得修改 VCPToolBox、不得创建 payload 或 enabled manifest。

    任何 precondition、sealed tuple、protected inventory、output suppression、ownership 或 cleanup
    失败必须 fail closed，只生成本包定义的 sanitized receipt 并停止。本决定不授权 commit、
    push、PR、merge、release、deploy、publish、tag、后续 Host-smoke 或下一阶段启动。

### B. Do not run

Retain the frozen R1 boundary and the v18.7 Jenn-only stop state. No Git object
command, temporary root, receipt, worktree, or Host operation may occur.

